{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured datauser with /srv/data as its home and a persistent ext4 filesystem quota of 100 MiB. Enforcement survived node1’s required restart and was re-proven with an oversized write.","actions_performed":["Installed quota-tools and created datauser plus /srv/data with mode 0700.","Enabled persistent usrquota mounting and an OpenRC quota activation service.","Set soft and hard block limits to 102400 KiB.","Verified oversized writes fail with “Quota exceeded,” both before and after restart.","Restarted node1; its boot ID changed and services, quota state, and checksumed data recovered."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"datauser is limited to 100 MB under /srv/data by the filesystem","command_ids":["cmd-bbdc8b48796442dc","cmd-8884814a10f648d2","cmd-69dd0ee977eb43eb","cmd-07e38332c2344261"],"summary":"Shows the account and protected directory, active 102400 KiB soft/hard ext4 quota, and filesystem rejection of 110 MiB writes before and after restart."},{"requirement":"Persistent quota configuration","command_ids":["cmd-5412a57c373d49b6","cmd-72af481d68b14154"],"summary":"Shows persistent fstab/OpenRC configuration and post-restart active user quotas with the expected limit."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-9504143a49f74816","cmd-bb466678a5554ac4","cmd-02202a9723ac4633","cmd-e9406e0ae2fa434a","cmd-72af481d68b14154","cmd-07e38332c2344261"],"summary":"Captures healthy pre-restart state and boot ID, restart acknowledgement, changed boot ID, recovered services, unchanged data checksum, active quota, and post-restart enforcement."}]}
